# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in real values. Never commit .env.
#
# Every environment variable the toolkit reads is listed here, with its default.
# A line that is not commented out may be left blank (blank means unset). A
# commented-out line keeps its default; uncomment it only to give it a real
# value, because a blank OPENCODE_AGENT, GIT_* name, RECOVER_FILE, RECOVER_ROUND
# or PORTING_KIT_FAULT is not the same as unset. Bun loads .env from the
# directory a script runs in, so run the toolkit's scripts from its root.
# tests/doc-claims.test.ts keeps this file and the code in step.

# --- Dex (durable execution engine) ---
# gRPC address of the Dex server started by `dexcli dev` (brew install superdurable/tap/dexcli).
# The worker, the demo commands, scripts/render-metrics.ts, the dashboard and the
# kill watcher all use it.
DEX_SERVER_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1:8801
# Worker endpoint that startFlow advertises to the Dex server. The worker also
# binds this address unless DEX_WORKER_BIND is set, so changing it moves the
# listener with it.
DEX_WORKER_TARGET=127.0.0.1:8803
# Address the worker listens on. Default: DEX_WORKER_TARGET, else 127.0.0.1:8803.
# Set it only when the listener differs from the advertised target, for example
# 0.0.0.0:8803 behind a remote DEX_WORKER_TARGET.
# DEX_WORKER_BIND=
# A blob cache is never shared across processes, so every process that opens one
# has its own directory (relative to where it runs), and the defaults are
# siblings, none inside another; all of them are gitignored (.dex-cache*/). Do
# not point two processes at one directory.
# Native blob cache of `run-demo.ts worker`. Default: .dex-cache
# DEX_BLOB_CACHE_DIR=.dex-cache
# Native blob cache of the other run-demo commands (demo, round, recover, ...),
# which run while the worker does. Default: .dex-cache-client
# DEX_CLIENT_BLOB_CACHE_DIR=.dex-cache-client
# (The dashboard and the kill watcher have their own: STATUS_BLOB_CACHE_DIR,
# DEX_WATCH_BLOB_CACHE_DIR.)
# The dexcli binary every script that queries Dex shells out to. Default: dexcli.
# DEXCLI_BIN=dexcli

# --- OpenCode (agent harness server) ---
# Base URL of `opencode serve`.
OPENCODE_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4096
# Default model for generic round trips (`run-demo.ts agent-roundtrip`) and probe
# sessions. Both must be set to take effect; otherwise the server's default model
# is used. Port-flow turns ignore these and use the lanes below.
OPENCODE_MODEL_PROVIDER=
OPENCODE_MODEL_ID=
# Default OpenCode agent for turns. Unset = the server's default agent.
# Leave it commented out rather than blank.
# OPENCODE_AGENT=
# OpenCode agent for reviewer sessions only, for example `plan` (a read-only
# agent) so reviewers cannot write even if the tool deny list is ignored.
# Unset = OPENCODE_AGENT or the server default.
# OPENCODE_REVIEWER_AGENT=
# How long to keep polling for an assistant reply that arrived without token
# usage, in milliseconds. Default: 900000 (15 minutes). A value that is not a
# whole number, is <= 0, or exceeds 24 hours uses the default.
# OPENCODE_PROMPT_WAIT_MS=900000
# Hard ceiling on one session.prompt call, in milliseconds; a call that outlasts
# it fails retryably so Dex re-dispatches the step. Default: 1200000 (20 minutes).
# Used exactly as written; the same validity rule as OPENCODE_PROMPT_WAIT_MS.
# OPENCODE_PROMPT_CALL_TIMEOUT_MS=1200000

# Port-flow turns route by lane. Values use providerID/modelID, split at the first
# slash (nano-gpt/openai/gpt-6-luna is provider nano-gpt); a value that does not
# parse is ignored and the default stands. src/harness/lanes.ts holds the routing.
# Defaults: planner zai-coding-plan/glm-5.3 @ high;
# executor zai-coding-plan/glm-5.3-flash @ max;
# reviewer nano-gpt/openai/gpt-6-luna @ high.
# Configure credentials for every effective lane in OpenCode, or override all
# three model variables with providers and models available in your environment.
# A *_VARIANT of `none` (any case) sends no variant, for a model that has no
# reasoning-effort levels.
OPENCODE_PLANNER_MODEL=
OPENCODE_PLANNER_VARIANT=
OPENCODE_EXECUTOR_MODEL=
OPENCODE_EXECUTOR_VARIANT=
OPENCODE_REVIEWER_MODEL=
OPENCODE_REVIEWER_VARIANT=
# Review turns on attempt 2 and later (a retry) are demoted to this model.
# Unset = the executor lane. The variant defaults to the reviewer lane's;
# `none` sends no variant.
OPENCODE_REVIEWER_MODEL_FALLBACK=
OPENCODE_REVIEWER_MODEL_FALLBACK_VARIANT=

# --- TypeSafe (Jev judgments) ---
# Enables billed, live TypeSafe judgments. Blank means a scripted offline double:
# no model judges anything, each symbol-table row takes the first recalled
# candidate and is tagged UNVERIFIED for the planner, and verdict-check,
# prioritize and vitest triage use their deterministic defaults.
# scripts/jev-spot-check.ts needs a key.
TYPESAFE_API_KEY=
# Force the scripted offline double even when a key is set. Any value except
# unset, blank, 0 or false turns it on.
# TYPESAFE_OFFLINE=
# The TypeSafe SDK itself also reads TYPESAFE_BASE_URL, TYPESAFE_DEFAULT_MODEL
# and TYPESAFE_LOG_LEVEL; this repository does not.

# --- Status dashboard (scripts/serve-status.ts, `bun run dashboard`) ---
# Read-only. Numeric values are validated; an invalid one falls back to the
# default with a warning at startup.
# Port. `run-demo.ts demo --dashboard` also uses it.
# STATUS_PORT=4646
# Deprecated fallback for STATUS_PORT, read only when STATUS_PORT is unset. Prefer
# STATUS_PORT: PORT is a generic name that other tools set.
# PORT=
# Bind address. The server has NO authentication, so keep a loopback address; a
# non-loopback value warns and needs STATUS_ALLOWED_HOSTS.
# STATUS_HOST=127.0.0.1
# Comma-separated hostnames accepted in the Host header, besides loopback names
# and the bind address (DNS-rebinding guard).
# STATUS_ALLOWED_HOSTS=
# The port TARGET repository whose commits and worktrees the dashboard shows.
# Default: the directory the server runs in.
# STATUS_REPO_ROOT=
# Flows that get state and history queries (newest port.Project parents are
# always kept, and so is every SubFlow port.File child of the newest run, up to
# 128: their verdicts and usage live there), and the SubFlow children of OTHER
# runs within that budget.
# STATUS_MAX_FLOWS=12
# STATUS_MAX_CHILD_FLOWS=8
# 0 = poll dexcli only: no SDK stream client and no blob cache.
# STATUS_STREAM_SUBSCRIBE=1
# The stream client's own blob cache. Default: .dex-cache-dashboard (gitignored).
# STATUS_BLOB_CACHE_DIR=.dex-cache-dashboard
# Comma-separated kill-event sidecar paths, relative to where the server runs.
# Default: metrics/kill-events.jsonl,metrics/kill-events.json,kill-events.json
# KILL_EVENT_FILES=
# Comma-separated burn-down files.
# Default: metrics/burn-down.json,metrics/burn-down.jsonl
# BURN_DOWN_FILES=

# --- Kill watcher (scripts/watch-queue-verify.ts) ---
# Blob cache of the watcher's own stream client. Default: .dex-cache-watch
# (gitignored). It never reads DEX_BLOB_CACHE_DIR.
# DEX_WATCH_BLOB_CACHE_DIR=.dex-cache-watch

# --- Git identity for toolkit commits ---
# Every git command the toolkit runs, including its commits in the output
# repository, sets these four. The defaults are porting-toolkit and
# toolkit@localhost. Because the environment outranks git config, your
# user.name and user.email do not apply to those commits unless you set them here.
# GIT_AUTHOR_NAME=porting-toolkit
# GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=toolkit@localhost
# GIT_COMMITTER_NAME=porting-toolkit
# GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL=toolkit@localhost

# --- run-demo.ts: recovery drill and fault injection ---
# `run-demo.ts recover` (the phase-0 probe recovery, not recover-port) reads these
# as the defaults of its --harness, --file and --round flags; a flag wins.
# Harness for recover: stub, opencode or auto (default auto; recover requires the
# real server unless this is `stub`).
# HARNESS=
# File and round that recover re-dispatches. Defaults: src/a.php and 1. A round
# that is not a whole number >= 1 is a usage error (exit 64).
# RECOVER_FILE=src/a.php
# RECOVER_ROUND=1
# TEST-ONLY fault injection, read by the worker so a recovery can be rehearsed;
# `worker --fault <spec>` overrides it. A spec that is not one of the kinds below,
# or belongs to the other flows (--flows), is a usage error (exit 64): it would
# never fire. Probe flows: commit:post-commit:<file>#<round>
# and agent-write:mid:<file>#<round> (the worker kills itself at that point).
# Port flows: symbol-table:post:seed (the worker kills itself after the symbol
# table) and queue-verify:inject-error:seed (the first verification adds one
# synthetic, labelled tsc error so a fix round runs). Never set it for a real
# migration.
# PORTING_KIT_FAULT=

# --- Ambient ---
# TMPDIR (the operating system's temp directory) holds run-demo's dashboard log
# ($TMPDIR/run-demo-dashboard-<port>.log) and the git-selftest repository.
